                    target=\"_blank\"\n                                       class=\"btn view-btn btn-sm\">\n                                        View Brochure\n                                    <\/a>\n                                \n                                <a target=\"_blank\"\n                                   href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-science-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                   class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm\">\n                                    Learn More\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Basic Eligibility for Data Analytics Course<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Before enrolling in a data analytics course, it is important to understand the basic eligibility requirements. These criteria help you know whether you are ready to start learning and build a strong foundation in data analytics.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1654\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/basic-data-analytics-course-eligibility.webp\" alt=\"Basic Eligibility for Data Analytics Course\" class=\"wp-image-20451\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/basic-data-analytics-course-eligibility.webp 1654w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/basic-data-analytics-course-eligibility-300x181.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/basic-data-analytics-course-eligibility-1024x619.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/basic-data-analytics-course-eligibility-768x464.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/basic-data-analytics-course-eligibility-1536x929.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1654px) 100vw, 1654px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Educational Qualification<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Most data analytics courses require candidates to have completed at least 10+2 or a bachelor\u2019s degree in any stream. Students from science, commerce, or arts backgrounds can apply, as no specific degree is strictly required.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Minimum Percentage Requirements<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>There is usually no strict minimum percentage required for most data analytics courses, especially online programs. However, some universities or institutes may require around 50% marks in previous qualifications for admission.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Age Limit<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>There is generally no age limit for enrolling in a data analytics course. Students, graduates, and working professionals of any age can start learning data analytics and build a successful career in this field.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can Non-Technical Students Learn Data Analytics?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Yes, non-technical students can easily learn data analytics. You do not need a strong programming or technical background to start. Many beginners come from commerce, arts, or other non-technical fields and successfully build careers in data analytics.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can begin with basic concepts like data understanding, simple calculations, and gradually move to advanced topics. With consistent practice and the right learning approach, anyone can develop the required skills step by step.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Today, many courses are designed especially for beginners, making it easier for non-technical students to learn and grow in the data analytics field.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Is Coding Required for Data Analyst Courses?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Coding is not always mandatory to start learning data analytics. Many beginner-level courses focus on tools like Excel, Power BI, and Tableau, where you can analyze data without writing complex code. This makes it easier for beginners and non-technical learners to get started.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>However, having basic knowledge of <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-programming-languages\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">programming languages<\/a> like <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Python<\/a> or <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/sql\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SQL<\/a> becomes helpful as you progress. It allows you to work with large datasets, automate repetitive tasks, and perform more advanced data analysis efficiently.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In simple terms, you can start your data analytics journey without coding, but learning basic programming skills will help you grow faster and open more career opportunities in the future.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Eligibility for Different Types of Data Analytics Courses<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Different data analytics courses have different eligibility criteria depending on their level. Below is the data analyst course eligibility required to start learning and build a successful career in this field.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Course Type<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Eligibility Criteria<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Certificate Courses<\/td><td>Open to all; basic education (10th\/12th) is enough, no strict academic requirements.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Diploma Courses<\/td><td>Requires 10+2 qualification from a recognized board; basic knowledge of computers is helpful.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Undergraduate Courses<\/td><td>Requires 10+2 with at least 50% marks; mathematics or statistics is preferred but not always required.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Postgraduate Courses<\/td><td>Requires a bachelor\u2019s degree in any field; some institutes may prefer math, IT, or commerce background.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>You can join our <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Mentorship Program<\/a> and become a job-ready Data Analyst in 14 weeks, helping you build practical skills and start your career with confidence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>\n                <p>Attend our live classes led by experienced and desiccated instructors of Wscube Tech.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"owl-carousel myOwl\">\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cracking-meta-google-ads-2026-data-automation-attribution?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-07-31T112145_393_1785491880854_775860.webp\" alt=\"Cracking Meta &amp; Google Ads 2026 - Data, Automation &amp; Attribution\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/ai-engineering-roadmap-2026?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-07-31T123426_340_1785490284771_211381.webp\" alt=\"AI Engineering Roadmap 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/how-to-build-an-ai-agent-from-scratch?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-03T133829_740__1__1786010890597_768466.webp\" alt=\"How to Build an AI Agent from Scratch \" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/soc-analyst-career-demand-in-2026?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-04T111115_404_1786011909630_974751.webp\" alt=\"SOC Analyst Career Demand in 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/booming-digital-marketing-career-in-ai-era?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-07T104930_382_1786105407836_186872.webp\" alt=\"Booming Digital Marketing Career in AI Era\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cybersecurity-professional-career-roadmap-2026-2?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-05T122121_005_1786351858212_930412.webp\" alt=\"Cybersecurity Professional Career Roadmap 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Skills Required to Become a Data Analyst<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>After understanding the eligibility for a data analyst course, it is important to know the key <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-skills\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">data analyst skills<\/a> needed to work with data, analyze information, and make better business decisions. Below are the essential skills required to become a data analyst:<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1654\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/data-analyst-skills.webp\" alt=\"Skills Required to Become a Data Analyst\" class=\"wp-image-20453\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/data-analyst-skills.webp 1654w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/data-analyst-skills-300x181.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/data-analyst-skills-1024x619.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/data-analyst-skills-768x464.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/data-analyst-skills-1536x929.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1654px) 100vw, 1654px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Technical Skills<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Data Analysis:<\/strong> Ability to collect, clean, and interpret data to find useful insights, helping businesses make better decisions based on accurate and meaningful information.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Excel\/Spreadsheet:<\/strong> Strong knowledge of spreadsheets to organize data, perform calculations, use formulas, pivot tables, and create reports for effective data analysis.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>SQL:<\/strong> Helps you query databases, retrieve specific data, and manage large datasets efficiently for analysis and decision-making.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Programming (Python or R):<\/strong> Basic knowledge of programming languages like Python or R to perform data analysis, automate tasks, and handle complex datasets more efficiently.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Visualization:<\/strong> Skill to present data using tools like Power BI and Tableau to create clear charts, graphs, and dashboards for better understanding.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Statistical Knowledge:<\/strong> Understanding basic statistics like mean, median, and probability to interpret data accurately and support strong data-driven decisions.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Soft Skills<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Communication Skills:<\/strong>&nbsp; Ability to explain data insights clearly to non-technical stakeholders, helping them understand results and make informed decisions based on data findings.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Problem-Solving:<\/strong> Strong thinking skills to identify issues, analyze data, and find effective solutions for real-world business problems using logical approaches.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Critical Thinking:<\/strong> Ability to evaluate data carefully, question assumptions, and make accurate decisions based on analysis.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Attention to Detail:<\/strong> Focus on accuracy while working with data to avoid errors and ensure reliable results.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Time Management:<\/strong> Helps you handle multiple tasks, meet deadlines, and complete data projects efficiently without compromising quality.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tools You Will Learn in a Data Analyst Course<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Below are the common <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">data analytics tools<\/a> you will learn in the course to work with data, analyze information, and create insights:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Tool<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Purpose<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Excel<\/td><td>Used for data cleaning, calculations, and basic analysis using formulas and charts.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SQL<\/td><td>Used to query databases, retrieve data, and manage large datasets efficiently.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Python<\/td><td>Used for data analysis, automation, and handling complex datasets.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Power BI<\/td><td>Used to create interactive dashboards and visualize data insights.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Tableau<\/td><td>Used for data visualization and building clear, interactive reports.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Google Sheets<\/td><td>Used for online data management, collaboration, and basic data analysis tasks.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The image below shows another example of how data analytics is used through a dashboard to track business performance. It includes key metrics like sales, products, earnings, and transactions, along with charts and graphs for monthly trends. These visual insights help businesses monitor growth, understand patterns, and make better data-driven decisions quickly and efficiently.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-analytics-dashboard.webp\" alt=\"How Data Analytics is used through a Dashboard\" class=\"wp-image-17891\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-analytics-dashboard.webp 1200w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-analytics-dashboard-300x225.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-analytics-dashboard-1024x768.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-analytics-dashboard-768x576.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>This dashboard clearly shows how data analytics simplifies complex data into easy visuals, helping users quickly understand performance and take informed actions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Career Opportunities After Learning Data Analytics<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>After learning data analytics, you can explore various <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-careers\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">data analytics careers<\/a> across industries; below are the opportunities:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Data Analyst:<\/strong> Analyze data, create reports, and find insights to help businesses make better decisions and improve overall performance across different departments and processes.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Business Analyst:<\/strong> Work with business teams to understand requirements, analyze data, and provide insights that help improve strategies, operations, and decision-making processes.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Scientist:<\/strong> Use advanced techniques, statistics, and programming to analyze large datasets, build models, and predict future trends for better business planning.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Engineer:<\/strong> Design, build, and manage data systems and pipelines to collect, store, and process large amounts of data for analysis.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Financial Analyst:<\/strong> Analyze financial data, track performance, and provide insights that help organizations manage budgets, investments, and financial planning effectively.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Marketing Analyst:<\/strong> Analyze customer data, campaigns, and market trends to help businesses improve marketing strategies and reach the right audience.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read<\/strong>: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-vs-data-scientist\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analyst vs. Data Scientist: Key Differences &amp; Comparison<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Future Scope of Data Analytics<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/future-of-data-analytics\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">future of data analytics<\/a> is growing rapidly as organizations increasingly rely on data for better decision-making. The global data analytics market is estimated to reach around USD <a href=\"https:\/\/www.fortunebusinessinsights.com\/data-analytics-market-108882\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">104.39 billion by 2026<\/a>, showing strong growth across industries.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It is further expected to reach approximately USD 495.87 billion by 2034, growing at a CAGR of around 21.5%. This rapid growth highlights excellent career opportunities, high demand, and long-term stability in the field of data analytics.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-1b17c912458ce3e8cbd0d868cb341198\"><strong>Explore More Data Guides<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/future-of-data-analytics\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Future Scope of Data Analytics<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-skills\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">In-Demand Data Analyst Skills<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-career-path\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Top Data Analyst Career Paths<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-job-description\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analyst Job Description<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-does-data-analyst-do\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">What Does a Data Analyst Do?<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/big-data-analytics-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Tools &amp; Software<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-project-ideas\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">20+ Data Analytics Projects<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-course-syllabus\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Course Syllabus<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/is-data-analyst-good-career\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Is Data Analyst A Good Career?<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/programming-languages-for-data-analytics\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Programming Languages<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Top Data Analytics Tools<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-analyst\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Become a Data Analyst<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Salary of a Data Analyst in India<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The salary of a data analyst in India depends on factors like experience, skills, location, and company. As demand for data professionals is increasing, companies are offering competitive salaries to skilled analysts across various industries.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Freshers can start with a decent salary, and with experience, their earnings grow significantly. By improving skills in data analysis and gaining practical experience, professionals can achieve higher salary packages over time.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Experience Level<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Average Salary (INR per year)<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Fresher (0\u20131 year)<\/td><td>\u20b93,00,000 \u2013 \u20b96,00,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1\u20133 Years<\/td><td>\u20b95,00,000 \u2013 \u20b910,00,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3\u20135 Years<\/td><td>\u20b98,00,000 \u2013 \u20b915,00,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>5+ Years<\/td><td>\u20b912,00,000 \u2013 \u20b925,00,000+<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Read in Detail<\/strong>: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-salary-india\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analyst Salary in India (Freshers &amp; Experienced)<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Start Learning Data Analytics?&nbsp;<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Starting data analytics requires a clear plan, basic understanding of concepts, and consistent practice to build strong skills and gain confidence in real-world data analysis tasks.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 1: Understand the Basics<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Start by learning what data analytics is and why it is important. Understand basic concepts like types of data, data collection methods, and how data is used to support better decision-making processes.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 2: Learn Essential Tools<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Start with beginner-friendly tools like Excel for basic analysis, then move to SQL for databases and tools like Power BI or Tableau for data visualization and dashboards.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 3: Learn Basic Programming<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Gain basic knowledge of Python or R to handle large datasets, automate tasks, and perform deeper data analysis efficiently in real-world projects and scenarios.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 4: Work on Projects<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Practice by working on real-world datasets and projects. This helps you apply your knowledge, improve problem-solving skills, and build a strong portfolio for job opportunities.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 5: Build a Portfolio<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Create a portfolio showcasing your projects, dashboards, and analysis work. This helps you clearly show your skills and increases your chances of getting hired for data analytics roles.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 6: Apply for Jobs<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Start applying for internships or entry-level data analyst roles to gain practical experience. Prepare for interviews, improve your communication and problem-solving skills, and continue learning new tools and techniques to grow in your data analytics career.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read<\/strong>: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-roadmap\/\">Data Analyst Roadmap: Step-by-Step Guide for Beginners<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Learn Data Analytics with WsCube Tech<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are looking to start or grow your career in data analytics, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">WsCube Tech<\/a> offers an <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-analytics-course?utm_source=WsB